{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And might</b> — Might and glory belong to a king who loves justice." "And the sense of <b>you alone</b> — or: from you, [at] the beginning." "And the sense of <b>uprightness</b> — they are the judgments of the Torah and its righteousness, which was given through his emissaries, and they are: Moses — <b>among his priests</b>: the word <i>kohen</i> throughout Scripture [means] one who serves, [as in] <b>the priests of YHWH</b> [means] the servants of our Elohim, and <b>he ministered to me</b>. Therefore if Aaron was the chief priest, Moses was the priest of priests, for he served during the seven days of ordination. And he mentioned Samuel, who was of their families, in his calling upon HaShem, and He answered him, as it is written: <b>I call upon YHWH and He answers me</b>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 99, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:36.659037075Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}